WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.770
<i>Wealth, fame, power...</i>

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.670
<i>Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates,</i>

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.970
<i>attained everything
this world has to offer.</i>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.840
<i>The words he uttered just before
his death drove people to the seas.</i>

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.680
<i>My treasure? If you want it,
you can have it!</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>Find it! I left everything
this world has to offer there!</i>

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.590
<i>And so men head for the Grand Line
in pursuit of their dreams!</i>

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.490
<i>The world has truly entered
a Great Pirate Era!</i>

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.860
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.770
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>ONE PIECE!</i>

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.620
<i>Compasses only cause delays</i>

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.350
<i>Delirious with fever,
I take the helm</i>

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:10.350
<i>If the dusty treasure map has
been verified, it's not a legend!</i>

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:18.170
<i>When it comes to personal storms,</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.480
<i>simply ride aboard
someone else's biorhythm</i>

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>and pretend it isn't there!</i>

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.650
<i>We're going to gather up
all our dreams</i>

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>and set out in search
of something to find</i>

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.600
<i>A coin in my pocket,
and do you wanna be my friend?</i>

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.970
<i>We are, We are on the cruise!</i>

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.040
<i>We are!</i>

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.310
<i>"Zeff and Sanji's Dream.
The Illusory All Blue."</i>

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.550
Ghin!!

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:10.320
No matter how incredible he was
in the past, he's now a mere cook.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.130
It's easy to blow his brains out.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.000
<i>You want to save this man,
right, Sanji-san?</i>

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Please, leave the ship without a fight.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.530
I don't want to kill you.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.840
Leave the ship?

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.150
No way!

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.680
Man, do you look stupid,
you damn geezer.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.020
If you're like that, you can't set
a good example for the fighting cooks.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:42.690
Hmph! I don't need a lecture
from a little brat.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.030
Where do you get off calling me
"little brat", you damn bastard?!

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.700
Quit treating me like a kid already!

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.030
That darn Sanji...

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.870
He sure isn't gonna
forsake Owner, is he?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:56.370
Ghin! Point that gun at me.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.510
Are you stupid?! You'll die!

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.040
Maybe...

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.980
<i>Sanji-san... Why?!</i>

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:09.320
If you want to die so bad,
I'll kill you in a refined way...

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:15.820
Don't move if you don't want your
Owner's head blown off.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.390
The Absolutely Natural
Pearl... Surprise!

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.330
Sanji! Why aren't you dodging?!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:30.670
If I did, that damn underling
would pull the trigger.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.170
Why? If you abandon this restaurant,

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.680
everyone's life will be saved.
It's a no-brainer, isn't it?!

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.740
This restaurant is that
damn geezer's treasure!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.480
I took everything away
from that damn geezer...

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.550
His power...

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.290
His dream...

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:02.300
So... I don't want that damn
geezer to lose anything else!!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.640
Sanji! Watch out!!

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.810
Pearl... Cymbals!

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.970
Sanji!!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.720
--The All Blue?
--Yeah!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.520
It's a legendary sea.
It's definitely out there somewhere!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:31.670
Don't be silly! Though there
is a legend like that.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:37.670
Well, we're seafaring cooks, so we've
all dreamed of that sea at one point.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:42.340
Right? I'll definitely
find that sea some day!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.550
You say you'll find it, but...

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.520
Do you know what kind of place
the All Blue is to start with?

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.020
Yes, I do! Don't insult my intelligence!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.020
The East Blue, West Blue,
North Blue, and South Blue...

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.290
A sea where fish from
all four seas live...

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.160
That's the All Blue.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.160
To seafaring cooks,
that's an irresistible paradise!

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.470
That's my dream!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.210
Oh yeah! There's all sorts of seafood
from all over the world in that sea.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.780
Cooks would be itching for
the chance to show their skills!

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.980
Yeah. It's worth risking your
life to look for that sea.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.650
--That is, if such a sea exists...
--What?

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.990
There's no way a miracle sea
like the All Blue could exist...

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.990
It's obvious if you just
give it a little thought...

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:32.990
It's probably a big lie told by some
daydreaming cook somewhere...

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.800
Now, enough with the silly stories.
Go collect plates, Sanji!

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:45.010
Ahh... How wasteful...
leaving this much food...

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:49.010
This one has barely been touched.
I was sure they'd like it.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.850
Customers these days
sure are pampered.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.850
You guys stop eating
the customers' leftovers.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.480
I ditched food that
looked rotten earlier.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.160
Saying things like that shows you're
still just halfway to being a cook.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.630
Don't forget we're seafaring cooks.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:10.300
The sea is an unpredictable place,
so it's best not to waste food.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.430
Why don't you have some, too, huh?

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.170
I don't want it!

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:20.000
Everyone, please calm down!
Calm down!!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.310
Pirates!

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.150
Pirates?!

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:38.460
That ship is... The Cook Pirates...
Red Foot Zeff's ship!

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.550
So they came back
from the Grand Line!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:59.810
I take it you're the pirate captain
Red Foot Zeff. How can I help you?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.420
Steal!

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:06.680
Steal all the valuables from them!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.190
<i>Dammit! I'm not gonna be killed!</i>

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:16.960
<i>I'm not gonna be killed
by bastards like them!</i>

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.300
Whoa!

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.970
What's this kid?

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:24.310
Hey kid. Don't swing things
like that around. It's dangerous.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.940
I'm bleeding. It's a serious injury.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:31.650
Shut up! I'm not gonna be killed
by bastards like you!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:36.150
--Sanji!
--Stop it! Don't fight back!

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:39.990
Seems he's got a death wish.
Kill that brat already!

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.720
I don't want to die! If I'm
gonna be killed by you bastards,

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.490
I'd rather kill you first!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.330
Sanji!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:54.100
--Boy, you did it, Captain.
--You have no mercy.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:06.740
I'm not gonna die!

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.750
I...

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.450
I will find the All Blue some day!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.630
He said "All Blue!"

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.970
What an ambitious goal!

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:31.640
Captain, tell him... that it didn't
exist even in the Grand Line.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:35.010
That idiot! He's still
spouting that nonsense...

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.790
I'm not gonna...

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:54.320
I'm not gonna be killed by damn
pirates in a place like this!

00:08:55.330 --> 00:09:01.600
Captain! Let's withdraw!
This storm is bigger than we expected!

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.710
Okay guys! Hurry up
and take the treasure on board!

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.770
We're withdrawing!

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.790
--Sanji!
--Dammit!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.730
Captain!!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.200
That damn brat!

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.810
Captain!!

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:45.580
Why'd you do that for just one brat?!

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:24.140
So you've come to, little brat?
You're very lucky.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:26.810
Pirate! Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:32.350
There's no way you can move!
Whose kicks do you think you took?

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.790
What about the ships?

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.560
Who knows? The sea was very rough.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.360
I wouldn't be surprised if
they were completely destroyed.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.700
We're the only ones
who washed up here.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:47.030
There's no fruits or animals
on this rocky mountain.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:49.770
There're at least fish in the sea,

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:53.240
but since the rock has
been curved by the waves,

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.180
we won't be able to come back up
once we go down. Isn't that sad?

00:11:56.180 --> 00:12:01.320
Hmph! It's all your fault!
I'll kill you!

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.620
Just keep complaining. We have no
choice but wait for help anyway.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:08.090
If no one comes, we'll just
dry up and turn into skeletons.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:11.490
A skeleton?! I will...

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.660
That bag over there is your share.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.250
What?

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.800
That's the food that
luckily washed up here.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.670
It's 5 days worth of food
at most if you eat normally.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:28.800
Use your head and eat.
Good thing that we're both cooks.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:35.180
Wait a second! Is that your share?!

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:39.050
It's huge... at least three times
as large as mine!

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:50.160
Of course! I'm an adult.
My stomach is larger than yours.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:54.170
You should be grateful that
I'm even sharing food with you.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:57.900
Don't expect any pity from me.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.440
You damn geezer!

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.590
You watch the other side of the sea.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:15.320
As soon as you see a ship,
let me know.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.390
Until then, we won't
be in contact at all

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.890
because that'd be a waste of energy.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.330
Good luck.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.800
That damn geezer!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.470
I'm not gonna let him know
even if I see a ship.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.670
It'll be fine.
I have 5 days worth of food.

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:35.180
If I have 5 days, there'll definitely
be a ship or two passing by.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:40.810
But just in case, I'll divide
them up for 20 days for now.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:44.350
If I have 20 days, there'll
be a ship passing by for sure.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:49.120
It'll be all right.
I'll definitely survive. It's easy!

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.810
No ship passed by today.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.400
That's all right. I'll just have to
be patient for a couple more days.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.170
I don't wanna die...

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.230
This is the last piece of bread...
It's gotten moldy...

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:55.820
Ahh... How wasteful...
leaving this much food...

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.830
You guys stop eating
the customers' leftovers.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:02.460
I ditched food that
looked rotten earlier.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:05.470
Why don't you have some, too, huh?

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.900
I don't want it!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.950
My last piece of bread...

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:15.430
I wonder... if that damn
geezer already died...

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.490
He's still alive...

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.330
And there's food, too...

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.590
There's still that much...

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:44.930
There's that much food!

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.670
I'll take it no matter what.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:55.340
It was all his fault to begin with!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.280
I want to live!

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:08.480
What did you come here for,
little brat?!

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:13.450
Did you see a ship or something?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.300
I came to steal your food.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:25.000
If you think you can kill me, go ahead.
I'll die if I don't eat anyway.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.570
To think you to have this
much food all to yourself...

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.840
What?

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:53.790
Didn't I tell you that we wouldn't
be in contact until we saw a ship?

00:17:54.800 --> 00:18:00.140
Why? This is all treasure...

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:05.510
It's odd that we can't eat
when we have money.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:14.050
Hey... This bag is
filled with treasure...

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:22.760
What is this?!
What's the meaning of this?!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:26.730
Where's your food? You didn't
eat anything until today?

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.200
Hey! Say something!

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:43.010
What happened to your leg?

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.660
<i>That time...</i>

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:02.900
So it wasn't a dream...
In order to save me, you...

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:12.610
What about the food? Did you give
me all the food you had?

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.280
That's right.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:18.620
Without that leg, you won't be
able to be a pirate any more!

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:21.090
I guess...

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:24.290
Why? I didn't ask for your help!

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:28.420
I can't think of any reason
for you to be kind to me!

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:32.300
Why? Why did you?!

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:40.440
Because you...
you had the same dream as me.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.310
The All Blue...

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:47.250
But... even your men
said it doesn't exist...

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:49.120
Of course it does!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:52.320
When the time comes,
head to the Grand Line.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:55.820
The All Blue surely exists there.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:59.430
As you see, I can't
be a pirate any more,

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:02.730
but this time, you can go and find it.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.670
H-hey! Geezer, don't die!

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:11.810
Don't just do as you please
and die as you please!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:15.310
I wonder...

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:18.950
I wonder how many people
died cursing the sea...

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.350
the grandness of the sea...

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:27.850
I've experienced crises like
this where I couldn't eat.

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.360
And each time I wish...

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:34.690
that there was a restaurant
in the middle of the sea...

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:35.700
Restaurant?

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:39.170
Yeah. I was thinking that if
I could leave this place alive,

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:44.370
I'd build a restaurant as
my final purpose in life...

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:48.840
All right, then, I'll help
you do that. So don't die!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:52.850
Ha! It's impossible for
a weak little brat like you!

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.720
I'll become strong, too!

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:59.520
So... don't die!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.670
Hey!!

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.670
Help!! Help the geezer!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:24.610
Help the damn geezer!!

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:33.720
Hey!! Hey!! Hey...

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:49.540
That damn geezer gave up
his leg so that I could live.

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:51.600
Wha?!

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:57.740
I... I can't repay the damn
geezer for his kindness

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:01.040
unless I risk my life for him too!

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:10.960
<i>Why do you get up... Sanji-san?</i>

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:17.830
In order for this place to be
a restaurant as long as possible...

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:20.960
That idiot...
Is he trying to get killed?

00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:25.670
You damn brat!

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:29.480
Ha! That's such a refined line.

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:33.010
But this restaurant
will be closed now...

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:36.610
and it will change into a pirate ship!

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:42.360
Stop it, you idiot!
Keep your hands off of them!

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.520
What's he trying to do?!

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:49.700
Gum-Gum...

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:51.690
Battle-Axe!!

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:06.070
<i>When I was little, I had
a vision of a treasure map</i>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:17.220
<i>and I always searched
for that miraculous place</i>

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:24.390
<i>before someone else could
beat me to it</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:37.000
<i>If the world is going to change</i>

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:45.490
<i>before I can even attain my dream</i>

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:52.560
<i>then take me to the time
when I knew nothing</i>

00:23:52.560 --> 00:24:02.560
<i>so that my memories won't fade</i>
